# PAIR enum_decl x edge_rule+keyed. CLAUDE.md's open row says a top-level enum
# rel already IS a reusable named type. Probed here as the state-machine idiom:
# a keyed register whose state column is that named enum, written from an edge.
rel phase_v(idle(since: int) ; fetching(started: int)).
rel phase(endpoint: text, state: phase_v) key(1).
rel poll_due(endpoint: text, at: int) log keep(all).

phase(Endpoint, fetching(At)) <+ poll_due(Endpoint, At).
